# Conceptual Questions (BFS & Foundation Model Intuitions)
# =====================================================================
# 1. Why does FloodFill work?
#    Answer: FloodFill behaves like a Breadth-First Search (BFS) pixel traversal.
#            Starting at the seed pixel, it visits neighboring pixels and adds them
#            to the segment queue if their colors are within the loDiff/upDiff tolerance.
#            The propagation halts when color difference exceeds the tolerance boundaries.
#
# 2. Why does Segment Anything (SAM) outperform Classical FloodFill?
#    Answer: FloodFill relies solely on basic pixel intensity/color similarities.
#            SAM, however, is a deep neural network pre-trained on millions of images.
#            It possesses rich semantic context, understands boundary contours, can segment
#            shadowed or varied textures of the same object, and ignores noise.

